.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt XBPRETTY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xbpretty
.Nd friendlier front end for the xbps package manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Nm xbp
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Nm xbp-install
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Nm xbp-remove
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Nm xbp-upgrade
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Nm xbp-autoremove
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Nm xbp-update
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
previews an xbps transaction, prints a nala-style summary, asks once, and then
runs the underlying xbps command.
It wraps xbps-install, xbps-remove and xbps-query; it does not replace them.
One binary is installed under seven names: xbpretty plus the six aliases xbp,
xbp-install, xbp-remove, xbp-upgrade, xbp-autoremove and xbp-update.
The argv[0] name selects or fixes the command.
.Pp
Durable output is written to standard output.
Live, interactive and diagnostic output, including the confirmation prompt,
the progress widget, forwarded child output, hints, warnings and errors, is
written to standard error.
Standard input is read only for the confirmation prompt and for history
selectors that a subcommand accepts.
.Pp
The command surface, the flag table and the shell completions all derive from
one internal table, so a command that is not listed here does not exist.
Arguments after the option terminator are passed to xbps unchanged in both the
dry and the real run.
.Sh COMMANDS
Commands are grouped as transaction, discovery, history, fetch and tooling
commands.
Global options are accepted before or after the command, up to the option
terminator.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm install PKG...
install packages from repositories.
.It Cm remove PKG...
remove installed packages.
Aliases: uninstall.
.It Cm purge PKG...
remove packages and their configuration files.
.It Cm autoremove
remove orphaned packages.
.It Cm autopurge
remove orphaned packages and their configuration files.
.It Cm upgrade
upgrade all installed packages.
Undocumented aliases: up, dist-up.
.It Cm full-upgrade
upgrade all installed packages (same as upgrade).
Aliases: dist-upgrade.
.It Cm safe-upgrade
upgrade all installed packages (same as upgrade).
.It Cm update
refresh the repository index.
.It Cm download PKG...
download package archives into the current directory.
.It Cm clean
clean the package cache.
.It Cm list [PKG...]
list packages matching the given globs.
.It Cm search PATTERN...
search package names and descriptions.
.It Cm show PKG...
show package details.
Aliases: info.
.It Cm policy [PKG...]
show repository precedence and pinned packages.
.It Cm history [ID|last|info|show|undo|redo|clear]
list, inspect, undo, redo or clear transaction history.
.It Cm undo [ID|last]
revert a recorded transaction.
.It Cm redo [ID|last]
reapply a recorded transaction.
.It Cm fetch
rank Void mirrors and configure repositories.
.It Cm completion bash|zsh|fish
print a shell completion script.
.It Cm link [DIR]
create the six xbp symlinks in a directory.
.It Cm log [PKG...]
print the transaction log.
.It Cm moo
moo.
Hidden easter egg; not advertised by --help.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
Options are either global or accepted by the commands named in their
description.
A flag passed to a command that does not accept it is a usage error and exits
2.
.Ss Global options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm -h , --help
print this help.
Accepted on every command.
.It Cm -V , --version
print version information.
--version is accepted on every command.
At the root the short -V means --version; after list or search, -V means
--virtual and the long form --version is still available.
.It Cm -v , --verbose
print every xbps command before running it.
Accepted on every command.
.It Cm --debug
dump the resolved configuration.
Accepted on every command.
.It Cm --config Ar FILE
read FILE instead of the system and user config files.
Accepted on every command.
.It Cm --color Ar WHEN
colour output: auto, always or never.
Accepted on every command.
Values: auto, always, never.
.It Cm --no-color
never emit ANSI colour.
Accepted on every command.
.It Cm --tui
force the full-screen interface.
Accepted on every command.
.It Cm --no-tui
disable the full-screen interface.
Accepted on every command.
.It Cm --history-dir Ar DIR
read history from DIR.
Accepted on every command.
Hidden from --help.
.El
