.Sh STREAMS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It standard output
Durable output only: the summary, Nothing to do., update counts, discovery
rows and NDJSON, download results, the fetch table, --help, --version and
completion scripts.
In Tui mode the transaction summary screen is the screen and standard output
is empty for that transaction.
.It standard error
Everything live, interactive or diagnostic: the prompt, progress widget,
verbose lines, forwarded child output, plan output, notices, warnings, hints
and errors.
.It standard input
Answers the confirmation prompt, carries full-screen keystrokes when a TUI
surface is active, and is inherited by xbps children.
A non-terminal stdin is never read as a prompt; use -y to proceed.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NO_COLOR
When set and non-empty, disables ANSI colour under color mode Auto.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Absolute base for the user configuration layer.
Ignored for an invoking sudo/doas user.
.It Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
Base for the transaction log.
Ignored for an invoking sudo/doas user.
.It Ev XBPRETTY_HISTORY_DIR
History directory, overridden by --history-dir.
.It Ev SUDO_USER , Ev DOAS_USER
Selects the invoking user's home for configuration and state.
.It Ev TERM , Ev COLUMNS
TERM=dumb disables the live UI; COLUMNS supplies the summary width when
standard output is not a terminal.
.It Ev HTTP_PROXY , Ev HTTPS_PROXY , Ev NO_PROXY
Proxy settings for predownload and fetch.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/xbpretty/config.toml
Optional system configuration layer, read before the user layer.
It is absent by default and the package never creates it.
.It Pa ~/.config/xbpretty/config.toml
User configuration layer, or
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xbpretty/config.toml
when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is an absolute path.
Under sudo or doas the invoking user's home is used.
.It Pa /var/lib/xbpretty/history/
Replayable history entries, one JSON file per transaction.
Override with --history-dir or XBPRETTY_HISTORY_DIR.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/xbpretty/transactions.log
Append-only audit log, falling back to
~/.local/state/xbpretty/transactions.log.
.It Pa /var/cache/xbps
The package cache used by predownload, download-only and undo/redo restores.
.It Pa /etc/xbps.d
xbps repository configuration written by fetch and clean --fetch, not xbpretty
configuration.
.It Pa /etc/xbps.d/*.xbpretty-backup
Pre-fetch copies of managed repository files, restored by clean --fetch.
.It Pa /usr/share/xbps.d
Read-only xbps repository configuration, read after /etc/xbps.d.
.It Pa /var/lib/xbpretty/fetch.json
The fetch manifest recording every file fetch wrote, its backup and its
SHA-256.
clean --fetch reads it.
.It Pa /usr/share/bash-completion/completions/xbpretty
Installed bash completion.
.It Pa /usr/share/zsh/site-functions/_xbpretty
Installed zsh completion.
.It Pa /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/xbpretty.fish
Installed fish completion.
.It Pa /usr/share/doc/xbpretty/config.toml.example
Canonical configuration example; it parses to the built-in defaults.
.It Pa /usr/share/doc/xbpretty/migration-rev6.md
Rev 5 to rev 6 migration guide.
.It Pa /usr/share/man/man8/xbpretty.8
This manual page, with the xbp.8, xbp-install.8, xbp-remove.8, xbp-upgrade.8,
xbp-autoremove.8 and xbp-update.8 alias links.
.It Pa /usr/share/man/man5/xbpretty.conf.5
The configuration manual page.
.It Pa /usr/share/licenses/xbpretty/LICENSE
The MIT licence.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm 0
Success, nothing to do, a dry run, a completed download-only run, clean,
update, discovery with no matches, history list/detail, or a successful fetch.
.It Cm 1
Refused confirmation, non-terminal stdin, non-root execution, missing package
arguments, runtime failure, missing or corrupt history, an unreplayable row, a
missing archive, an invalid prompt answer, a cancelled fetch, or a partial
download.
.It Cm 2
Usage error, conflicting flags, an N/A flag, invalid configuration,
--print-uris combined with another stop flag, or a TUI conflict.
Configuration errors reported by the loader also exit 2.
.It Cm 130
Interrupted by SIGINT.
.It other
An xbps child's exit status is passed through unchanged.
.El
.Sh SECURITY
When effective UID is 0, a privileged [Xbps] path from a configuration layer
is honoured only when the supplying file is a regular file owned by UID 0 with
no group or world write bit, checked on the descriptor that is read.
An untrusted path is ignored and never executed; one warning per key is
printed.
Non-privileged keys from the same layer still apply.
.Pp
Repository signatures are always verified by xbps.
xbpretty never disables signature checking and never installs packages itself.
A local undo/redo replay repository verifies only the SHA-256 of a cached
archive, relying on the signature verified when xbps downloaded it.
.Pp
The package installs no configuration file under /etc and no conf_files entry;
the optional system layer is administrator-created.
fetch writes repository lines under /etc/xbps.d as package-manager state.
.Sh SEE ALSO
xbpretty.conf(5)
.Pp
https://github.com/soubarnak/xbpretty
